    "body": "Fixes #43873\n\n## Motivation\n\nOn ComfyUI v0.39.2, every integrated-mode model (SGLDUNETLoader) fails to load. The node raises \"The SGLD worker exited while loading the model\", and the worker log shows:\n\n```\nFile \"ComfyUI/main.py\", line 25, in <module>\n  from app.database.db import ...\nFile \"ComfyUI/app/database/db.py\", line 9, in <module>\n  from utils.install_util import get_missing_requirements_message\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'utils.install_util'; 'utils' is not a package\n```\n\nThe worker is started with multiprocessing spawn, so the child re-imports the parent's `__main__`, which under ComfyUI is `main.py`. ComfyUI's `nodes.py` puts `ComfyUI/comfy` first on `sys.path`, so in the child `import utils.install_util` finds `comfy/utils.py` instead of ComfyUI's `utils/` package.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Hide `__main__.__file__` / `__spec__` only while `DiffGenerator.from_pretrained` starts the workers, then restore them. The worker never runs ComfyUI's entry script; it only needs sglang modules.\n- Regression test that spawns a real worker through `init_generator` from a host script that fails when re-imported, like ComfyUI's `main.py`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo change to model outputs. End to end check with ComfyUI v0.39.2 started the normal way (`python main.py`) and a Flux.1-dev SGLDUNETLoader workflow (1024x1024, 25 steps):\n\n- main, T4: the worker dies with the `'utils' is not a package` error above.\n- This branch, L40S: the worker starts and the workflow completes.\n\n![Flux.1-dev via SGLD on this branch](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OnePunchMonk/sglang/8cbd16e2df5c03958295216505fca001bdb44ce8/spawnfix_flux_l40s_plain_launch.png)\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). The new test fails on main and passes here; `test_comfyui_generator.py`, `test_comfyui_adapters.py`, `test_comfyui_session.py`: 59 passed on a T4.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38280102285](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38280102285)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38280101950](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38280101950)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38280102570](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38280102570)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
